{:spec/title "Ariadne step 1a: one clause vocabulary for severity and enforcement"

 :spec/description
 "Create component policy-clause: the single definition site for the
  severity scale and the enforcement-action vocabulary, as the ground
  layer for Ariadne PolicyClause labels.

  GROUP 1: The vocabulary component
  New component policy-clause exposing: the severity scale
  [:critical :high :medium :low :info] with total order; the
  enforcement actions [:hard-halt :require-approval :warn :audit]
  documented as relaxation modes (hard-halt = no relaxation;
  require-approval = approval workflow; warn/audit = envelope
  obligations); Malli schemas for both; predicate + comparator fns
  that REJECT unknown values with an anomaly instead of defaulting.

  GROUP 2: Collapse the copies
  schema/supervisory.clj violation-severities and evidence-bundle
  schema.clj violation-severities are deleted; both namespaces (and
  policy-pack RuleSeverity) become interface pass-throughs to
  policy-clause. schema/core.clj severities moves behind the same
  interface. No duplicate literal vocabularies survive anywhere
  (grep-clean acceptance below).

  GROUP 3: Kill the silent ordering default
  compare-severity's unknown->rank-99 default is replaced: comparing
  or filtering on an unknown severity returns an anomaly (fail-loud).
  All call sites swept in the same change - no eventually-consistent
  drift window.

  GROUP 4: The mechanical axis stays, mapped
  The gate-classification mechanical scale [:error :warning :note
  :none] is a different axis (tool exit semantics, not policy
  severity). It stays, but policy-clause owns the one explicit
  mapping fn mechanical->severity, and gate/pre_verify_lint.clj's
  cross-vocabulary default (:rule/severity :high into a mechanical
  path) is rewritten through that mapping."

 :spec/intent {:type :feature
               :scope ["components/policy-clause/"
                       "components/schema/src/ai/miniforge/schema/core.clj"
                       "components/schema/src/ai/miniforge/schema/supervisory.clj"
                       "components/policy-pack/src/ai/miniforge/policy_pack/schema.clj"
                       "components/evidence-bundle/src/ai/miniforge/evidence_bundle/schema.clj"
                       "components/gate/src/ai/miniforge/gate/pre_verify_lint.clj"]}

 :spec/constraints
 ["One definition site; every other namespace is an interface pass-through (DRY per component+interface rule)"
  "Unknown severity or enforcement value anywhere = anomaly, never a default rank, never a silent drop"
  "Run the FULL test suite, not affected-only: schema components have dependents the affected-tests selector misses"
  "No compat shims: the deleted duplicate defs are deleted, not deprecated"
  "Stratified design, max 3 layers per file"]

 :spec/acceptance-criteria
 ["grep for the severity vector/set literals finds exactly one definition site (policy-clause) outside tests"
  "compare/rank on an unknown severity returns an anomaly; a test proves the old sort-last behavior is gone"
  "policy-pack, supervisory, evidence-bundle schemas validate against the shared vocabulary via pass-through"
  "mechanical->severity is the only crossing between the mechanical axis and the policy axis; pre_verify_lint uses it"
  "full bb test green"]

 :spec/priority
 {:tier :blocker
  :axes #{:governance-credibility :policy-enforcement}
  :theme :ariadne-adoption
  :rationale "Every later Ariadne artifact (clause labels, envelopes, decide()) speaks this vocabulary; five definition sites and a sort-last default make fail-closed unrepresentable today."
  :blocks ["ariadne-decision-envelope.spec.edn"]
  :blocked-by []}

 :spec/workflow-type :canonical-sdlc}
